{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And to the man.</b> Rabbi Yehuda ben Rabbi Simon said: from בראשית until ולאדם there are seventy-one mentions of the divine name, corresponding to the seventy-one of the Sanhedrin — teaching that HaShem judged him with a Great Sanhedrin to impose death upon him. And if you ask: are there not seventy-three? Rather, 'בצלם אלהים' and 'והייתם כאלהים' are not included, as I explained above." "<b>And to the man He said.</b> All serve face corresponding to back, except for three that serve face corresponding to face, because the Shekhinah speaks with them, and they are: the serpent, the fish. The man — as it is written ולאדם אמר; the serpent — ויאמר ה׳ אלהים אל הנחש; the fish — as it is said ויאמר ה׳ לדג." "<b>Because you listened to the voice of your wife.</b> And not to My voice — and she revealed to you the serpent's secret; therefore you were not inadvertent, and therefore you were punished." "<b>Cursed is the ground.</b> The ground was cursed because it transgressed the command of HaShem, who said to it: תדשא הארץ עץ פרי עושה פרי — just as the fruit is eaten, so the tree should be edible; but it did not do so, rather: ותוצא הארץ עץ עושה פרי. And it was cursed only for the days of the man's life, as it is said: כל ימי חייך. Go and reckon his years and you will find that from the death of the man until the birth of Noah — no one was born until Noah was born, and the blessing returned to its place, as it is written: זה ינחמנו ממעשנו ומעצבון ידינו מן האדמה וגו׳, and it is written: ויחל נח איש האדמה ויטע כרם." "<b>For your sake.</b> For your produce — from the language of traversing the land, as it writes after it: וקוץ ודרדר תצמיח לך." "<b>All the days of your life.</b> And if you ask: how was Adam saved from death, when it is written ״כי ביום אכלך ממנו מות תמות״? One may answer: he was saved because he returned straightforward words — ״האשה אשר נתת עמדי״ etc. — I had assumed that You did not give me a wife except for my own betterment, and I had no need to be on guard against her. Even so, because he neglected the commandment, he was cursed."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:51.890785736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}